  "preamble": "Word-initial change of the palatal glide [j] to the glottal fricative [h], a debuccalization with devoicing. In Greek one set of Proto-Indo-European initial *y- became h- (*yóh₁r̥ 'year, season' > ὥρα hṓrā; Proto-Hellenic *yêkʷər > ἧπαρ hêpar 'liver'; *Hyós > ὅς hós 'who'), while another set became z- (ζυγόν 'yoke'). The aspirate is written in Attic and later lost (Modern Greek ήπαρ ípar).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Debuccalization, Devoicing",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Ancient Greek",
      "languageFamily": "Hellenic",
      "examples": [
